1
00:00:00,940 --> 00:00:05,190
Om namo bhagavate vasudevaya.

2
00:00:10,130 --> 00:00:15,450
[Listen. He is chanting Sanskrit. It sounds like "ato 'rhatah sthavaratam," and the rest is not clear.]

3
00:00:17,530 --> 00:00:23,430
[Listen. The Sanskrit verse continues, and the wording is not clear.]

4
00:00:25,540 --> 00:00:33,220
[Listen. The Sanskrit continues. It sounds like "smaranam prasadena, tatrapi mad-anugrahat," and the rest is not clear.]

5
00:00:35,880 --> 00:00:38,420
Vasudevasya sannidhyam.

6
00:00:40,750 --> 00:00:43,490
[Listen. Sanskrit. It sounds like "labdhva divya-sarac-chate," and the rest is not clear.]

7
00:00:46,550 --> 00:00:48,170
[Listen. Sanskrit. It sounds like "vritteshvara-lokatam," and the rest is not clear.]

8
00:00:52,460 --> 00:00:56,080
Again,

9
00:00:58,360 --> 00:01:01,760
they will receive devotion in the future.

10
00:01:07,130 --> 00:01:14,510
This is how Narada Muni is giving a curse to Nalakuvara and Manigriva.

11
00:01:15,580 --> 00:01:23,880
It is spoken in two verses. Ato 'rhatah sthavaratam. These

12
00:01:23,880 --> 00:01:32,060
are the sons of a lokapala, the sons of Kuvera, and they have become so careless

13
00:01:32,060 --> 00:01:39,220
after drinking that they do not even know they are naked.

14
00:01:42,110 --> 00:01:50,480
So for this bad act they will receive a tree's body. They are fit to become immovable.

15
00:01:50,480 --> 00:01:53,080
They are fit for it. They are worthy of it.

16
00:01:54,540 --> 00:02:02,980
Just as trees stay naked, and do not feel it,

17
00:02:05,060 --> 00:02:06,880
this is Narada's curse.

18
00:02:09,940 --> 00:02:18,680
But along with it he is giving mercy. Tatrapi mad-anugrahat.

19
00:02:19,980 --> 00:02:24,660
Even in a tree's body, by my mercy,

20
00:02:26,610 --> 00:02:28,510
memory will remain.

21
00:02:32,100 --> 00:02:38,360
They will keep the memory of which wrong made them trees, and

22
00:02:41,460 --> 00:02:49,540
[Listen, around 2:41. A few words are unclear.] They will remember even after becoming trees.

23
00:02:49,600 --> 00:02:57,750
And my special mercy will be on them. After one hundred years of the demigods have passed,

24
00:02:57,750 --> 00:03:02,710
they will see Lord Krishna directly. They will see Him face to face.

25
00:03:05,160 --> 00:03:10,780
And they will get their own form back. They will be freed.

26
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:24,180
In this way,

27
00:03:24,180 --> 00:03:32,340
sometimes an insect body, sometimes a bird, sometimes a human, sometimes a demigod. The wheel of this world keeps turning.

28
00:03:32,340 --> 00:03:40,860
It keeps turning. But if, by some cause, by the Lord's mercy, a person

29
00:03:40,860 --> 00:03:56,720
is freed from birth and death, that is a very big thing. So Narada

30
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:05,780
This is Narada Muni's Vaishnava heart. Seeing their fallen condition, he melted. Anger

31
00:04:05,780 --> 00:04:14,070
did not come. Sometimes a devotee may think Narada got angry at Nalakuvara and Manigriva.

32
00:04:15,570 --> 00:04:17,570
But this is very great mercy.

33
00:04:19,640 --> 00:04:23,180
Narada showed mercy. He did not show anger.

34
00:04:24,940 --> 00:04:32,060
He settled it. One hundred years from today they will see Krishna face to face.

35
00:04:34,390 --> 00:04:41,330
And even after entering a tree's body, they will always remember this birth.

36
00:04:44,010 --> 00:04:52,080
They will feel sorry for their own mistake, and the Lord's mercy will come. They will also

37
00:04:52,080 --> 00:04:54,060
keep hoping for it. So

38
00:04:56,140 --> 00:04:58,920
is this a curse, or a blessing?

39
00:05:00,760 --> 00:05:06,060
No ordinary person chasing enjoyment will be able to say this is a curse.

40
00:05:08,860 --> 00:05:17,120
This is the greatest blessing. The bondage of birth and death is cut, finished, and the Lord

41
00:05:17,120 --> 00:05:25,600
is reached. That is the highest success, isn't it? If they receive the Lord's service, then Nalakuvara

42
00:05:25,600 --> 00:05:33,800
and Manigriva will receive that service. Labdha-bhakti. They will receive the Lord's devotion. In the future

43
00:05:33,900 --> 00:05:41,940
this will happen. Labdha-bhakti bhavishyatah. They will become people who receive

44
00:05:41,940 --> 00:05:48,900
devotion. They will receive the Lord's devotion. In the Damodarashtakam it is said,

45
00:05:50,040 --> 00:05:53,600
by Satyavrata Muni, in the Padma Purana,

46
00:05:55,960 --> 00:06:04,500
[Listen, 5:56 to 6:04. He is quoting the Damodarashtakam in Sanskrit, and several words are unclear.]

47
00:06:04,500 --> 00:06:06,940
and please give me prema-bhakti, just for Your happiness.

48
00:06:09,020 --> 00:06:22,040
Please give me Your devotion in the same way.

49
00:06:25,630 --> 00:06:33,670
So this is not a curse. Seeing their improper behavior, a little

50
00:06:33,670 --> 00:06:34,310
displeasure rose in him.

51
00:06:36,190 --> 00:06:44,350
He did not like it. Sons of such a great demigod, of such a great person,

52
00:06:44,350 --> 00:06:52,310
acting badly with women, and in such a great holy place, on Kailasa, by the Ganga.

53
00:06:53,240 --> 00:07:01,310
For that he gave them a punishment. But it was not really punishment. It was actually a blessing.

54
00:07:01,430 --> 00:07:06,190
After Kailasa they took birth in the land of Braj,

55
00:07:07,550 --> 00:07:15,840
in Mahavana. And they received a body full of feeling for Krishna. Even as trees, they

56
00:07:15,840 --> 00:07:16,800
had Krishna-bhava.

57
00:07:18,210 --> 00:07:26,330
Again and again,

58
00:07:27,710 --> 00:07:33,470
the children played in their shade, and played hide

59
00:07:36,030 --> 00:07:44,100
and seek. They would get behind the trees. From one side the others would say, "Go find them," and they would search.

60
00:07:44,140 --> 00:08:00,620
They wanted to catch them. Lord Krishna would sometimes be on this side, sometimes on that side. So they

61
00:08:05,640 --> 00:08:13,920
This is a blessing. One day of the demigods equals six months for people like us.

62
00:08:13,920 --> 00:08:22,550
By that count, after one hundred years they will see Krishna. They will see Him directly.

63
00:08:22,550 --> 00:08:23,010
They will.

64
00:08:28,260 --> 00:08:41,540
Those hundred years are nothing. For how many years have we been lying in this world of illusion?

65
00:08:41,600 --> 00:08:49,790
The stream of a soul's births, this bondage, is beginningless. Who knows for how many years we

66
00:08:49,790 --> 00:08:52,810
have been taking birth again and again, and

67
00:08:56,170 --> 00:09:02,150
we also do not know for how many years after this we will still have to take birth.

68
00:09:04,500 --> 00:09:09,420
In a single kind of body one may have to be born millions and millions of times.

69
00:09:11,600 --> 00:09:17,080
Narada settled it: after one hundred years of the demigods,

70
00:09:18,430 --> 00:09:21,770
Lord Krishna, on this

71
00:09:23,820 --> 00:09:30,460
earth, will descend, and in Mathura.

72
00:09:32,310 --> 00:09:40,390
He will perform pastimes in Braj, in Mahavana, and everywhere. Right there they will see the Lord directly.

73
00:09:40,390 --> 00:09:42,750
They will.

74
00:09:44,160 --> 00:09:52,750
After cursing those two brothers in this way, Narada

75
00:09:52,750 --> 00:09:59,060
now came from Alakapuri, from Kailasa, to Badrikashram.

76
00:10:01,240 --> 00:10:09,680
Why did he come to Badrikashram? One devotee writes that Narada thought, "In giving a curse, one's austerity

77
00:10:09,680 --> 00:10:10,660
gets spent."

78
00:10:12,500 --> 00:10:20,620
So one should go to Badrikashram to perform austerity. If wealth has been spent,

79
00:10:20,620 --> 00:10:28,840
one should gather it again, no? Narada thought, "I became angry. Two

80
00:10:28,840 --> 00:10:37,250
demigods I turned into trees, so my austerity was snatched away. Therefore

81
00:10:37,250 --> 00:10:45,450
he also went to Badrikashram to perform austerity again. Or, the worshipful Lord of Badrikashram is

82
00:10:45,450 --> 00:10:46,870
Lord Nara-Narayana.

83
00:10:49,460 --> 00:10:57,460
So Narada went to Them, to tell Them, "I threw Nalakuvara and

84
00:10:57,460 --> 00:11:02,020
Manigriva down from heaven and made them trees."

85
00:11:03,400 --> 00:11:15,360
[Listen, around 11:03. He starts a sentence and it breaks off.]

86
00:11:22,470 --> 00:11:30,660
Kailasa was nearby, so it was natural to come to Badrikashram. So

87
00:11:30,660 --> 00:11:38,840
he went to Badrikashram. And these two, Nalakuvara and Manigriva, took birth here,

88
00:11:38,840 --> 00:11:44,920
in Mahavana, in Nanda Baba's courtyard. So

89
00:11:55,250 --> 00:11:57,630
After that, when Lord Krishna

90
00:11:59,970 --> 00:12:07,810
was tied,

91
00:12:11,040 --> 00:12:13,740
the Bhagavatam says, to make true the words of the best of the Lord's devotees.

92
00:12:15,240 --> 00:12:23,500
Among all the Lord's devotees, Narada is the best. So, His devotee

93
00:12:23,500 --> 00:12:31,590
Narada's words, to make them true, the Lord slowly dragged the mortar toward the trees

94
00:12:31,590 --> 00:12:32,510
and began to go.

95
00:12:35,500 --> 00:12:45,880
[Listen, around 12:35. One short sound is unclear.]

96
00:12:46,430 --> 00:12:54,770
There stood the twin Arjuna trees, the two yamalarjuna trees.

97
00:12:54,770 --> 00:13:01,640
Their roots were very strong, very deep, and very thick.

98
00:13:03,210 --> 00:13:10,250
And the trees were very tall, and their shade spread far.

99
00:13:11,580 --> 00:13:19,320
[Listen, around 13:11. A short phrase is unclear.]

100
00:13:19,740 --> 00:13:19,740
[Listen, around 13:19. One word is unclear.]

101
00:13:21,690 --> 00:13:24,310
And the mortar was coming along behind.

102
00:13:31,650 --> 00:13:37,790
He went slowly, walking like a little child.

103
00:13:40,780 --> 00:13:45,600
Slowly, and He went while doing His child pastimes.

104
00:13:47,160 --> 00:13:55,300
It looked as if He was not going to deliver anyone. In His own trouble He was dragging the mortar

105
00:13:55,300 --> 00:14:03,500
along. A rope was tied at His waist, around His belly, and by that rope, behind Him,

106
00:14:03,500 --> 00:14:11,670
the mortar was tied. He started off slowly, so the mortar

107
00:14:11,670 --> 00:14:13,510
also went slowly.

108
00:14:15,700 --> 00:14:24,400
The Lord was tied to the mortar, but He could not untie Himself, and nobody else could untie Him. Mother

109
00:14:24,400 --> 00:14:32,740
Yashoda had warned the children, "Nobody will untie Him." And Krishna did not even have

110
00:14:32,740 --> 00:14:33,760
the courage to untie Himself.

111
00:14:35,610 --> 00:14:41,770
If He untied it, He was afraid He would get another spanking. So

112
00:14:44,170 --> 00:14:57,700
He could not untie it, and He was not able to, in the mood of a child.

113
00:15:01,860 --> 00:15:02,400
He is coming.

114
00:15:05,280 --> 00:15:14,370
This is a supremely charming sight of the Lord, as He goes slowly through the courtyard, dragging the mortar,

115
00:15:14,370 --> 00:15:15,450
slowly.

116
00:15:21,900 --> 00:15:30,460
The Lord thought, "Among the divine sages, Narada is most dear to Me. Very

117
00:15:30,460 --> 00:15:41,700
dear. Very dear." And

118
00:15:44,740 --> 00:15:48,200
whatever he has said, I will do it just like that.

119
00:15:52,070 --> 00:16:00,360
What that great soul, Narada,

120
00:16:00,360 --> 00:16:03,820
has said, I will do.

121
00:16:05,700 --> 00:16:13,900
He was thinking this in His mind, and dragging the mortar. He was remembering Narada. What Narada

122
00:16:13,900 --> 00:16:18,100
said, I will fulfill.

123
00:16:22,900 --> 00:16:30,900
See, the Lord could have delivered Nalakuvara even by His glance, just by looking. Still

124
00:16:30,900 --> 00:16:34,300
the Lord went, dragging the mortar.

125
00:16:42,380 --> 00:16:47,340
This is the Lord's nature. He fulfills the wishes of His devotees.

126
00:16:49,960 --> 00:16:52,340
And among the devotees, the chief is Narada.

127
00:16:56,310 --> 00:17:07,090
Narada.

128
00:17:12,500 --> 00:17:13,040
So, one time,

129
00:17:15,440 --> 00:17:20,300
a woman became a widow.

130
00:17:24,810 --> 00:17:28,510
People were carrying her husband to the cremation ground.

131
00:17:30,240 --> 00:17:38,670
The poor woman came crying and bowed at the Goswami's feet. Goswami Tulsidas,

132
00:17:38,670 --> 00:17:40,410
by his nature, said,

133
00:17:41,660 --> 00:17:44,920
"May your good fortune remain unbroken." And

134
00:17:46,390 --> 00:17:50,540
her husband had already died, and

135
00:17:53,770 --> 00:17:57,350
she began to weep. Then the Goswami asked, "Why are you crying?"

136
00:17:59,180 --> 00:18:02,120
Later he came to know that her husband had died.

137
00:18:07,310 --> 00:18:10,710
Then the Goswami thought, "Now

138
00:18:12,280 --> 00:18:14,200
my words must come true."

139
00:18:15,650 --> 00:18:23,820
At once he went to his altar, to Lord Rama, and said, "O Lord, from my mouth

140
00:18:23,820 --> 00:18:24,720
it came out."

141
00:18:26,880 --> 00:18:31,220
"May her good fortune remain," so her good fortune must remain.

142
00:18:33,640 --> 00:18:41,880
Saying only this, he took Ganga water that had become charanamrita, and

143
00:18:41,880 --> 00:18:50,020
he came. He asked and found out where the man was, the one who had died. He went there.

144
00:18:50,220 --> 00:18:58,410
He sprinkled the Lord's charanamrita on him, and the man

145
00:18:58,410 --> 00:19:00,970
sat up. So

146
00:19:04,400 --> 00:19:08,600
at that time the Goswami said, "This is not my greatness."

147
00:19:10,330 --> 00:19:18,490
"I am Your devotee. Please make my word true." So the Lord brought him back to life.

148
00:19:18,490 --> 00:19:21,110
This event is very well known. So

149
00:19:27,420 --> 00:19:32,420
Honoring His devotee's word, the Lord brought that person back to life.

150
00:19:34,860 --> 00:19:39,400
This is the Lord's nature. Narada

151
00:19:41,190 --> 00:19:49,510
is a great devotee. From Narada's mouth it came that these two must be delivered. They

152
00:19:49,510 --> 00:19:59,290
will see the Lord. They

153
00:20:00,980 --> 00:20:08,890
have to be delivered by this very mortar. That is why the mortar is going behind Him, dragging along.

154
00:20:16,400 --> 00:20:24,460
[Listen, around 20:16. He quotes a Sanskrit line about the best of the sages and the sons of the treasurer. The wording is not clear.]

155
00:20:25,120 --> 00:20:33,490
Thinking in this way, the Lord passed between the two Arjuna

156
00:20:33,490 --> 00:20:38,610
trees. The two trees were almost touching.

157
00:20:40,090 --> 00:20:47,850
And they were very big, very wide, very strong. Krishna passed between them.

158
00:20:48,630 --> 00:20:51,530
Krishna was a small child, so He got through.

159
00:20:52,870 --> 00:21:01,080
But the mortar coming behind was not straight. It had fallen sideways.

160
00:21:01,080 --> 00:21:02,600
It was lying across.

161
00:21:04,970 --> 00:21:08,110
So Krishna got through, but the mortar got stuck.

162
00:21:09,810 --> 00:21:12,370
[Listen. He is quoting "iti antarena arjunayoh krishnas tu," and the Sanskrit is unclear.]

163
00:21:14,160 --> 00:21:15,980
[Listen. The Sanskrit of this verse continues.]

164
00:21:18,600 --> 00:21:33,140
Between the two Arjuna trees,

165
00:21:33,200 --> 00:21:41,430
there was only as much room as Krishna could pass through. Not more. Only enough for Krishna

166
00:21:41,430 --> 00:21:44,550
to slip out.

167
00:21:47,850 --> 00:21:53,110
But the mortar had turned sideways.

168
00:21:56,420 --> 00:22:02,880
It was crosswise, so the mortar got stuck.

169
00:22:07,580 --> 00:22:17,230
And when the mortar stuck, that child pulled hard. Around His belly

170
00:22:17,230 --> 00:22:21,420
the rope was tied, so the pull came on His belly.

171
00:22:24,240 --> 00:22:26,700
That rope was not very strong.

172
00:22:28,100 --> 00:22:30,940
It was a very soft rope. Mother Yashoda had tied it.

173
00:22:32,790 --> 00:22:36,790
But whatever the Lord wants, that is what happens.

174
00:22:38,140 --> 00:22:44,540
He went on, dragging the mortar. He got through. The mortar got stuck between the two of them. So

175
00:22:46,050 --> 00:22:54,180
He pulled hard, with great force. He pulled from His

176
00:22:54,180 --> 00:22:55,560
waist.

177
00:22:58,500 --> 00:23:01,100
At that moment, if one could have seen it,

178
00:23:02,930 --> 00:23:11,960
if there had been a video then, one would have seen how Krishna was pulling. On His

179
00:23:11,960 --> 00:23:20,300
face the effort was showing. He was pulling very hard, from His waist, and

180
00:23:22,990 --> 00:23:26,450
He did not take some huge form. He was a child.

181
00:23:28,740 --> 00:23:36,300
A child was pulling the mortar.

182
00:23:39,350 --> 00:23:47,260
Then Damodara, the child with the rope around His belly, was pulling it.

183
00:23:51,670 --> 00:23:59,670
And just from His pulling, the roots of both trees came out together.

184
00:23:59,670 --> 00:23:59,970
They came out.

185
00:24:02,200 --> 00:24:10,270
They were very large trees, so their roots came out, roots that would not have come out even if thousands of elephants pulled.

186
00:24:10,270 --> 00:24:18,610
Both trees came out.

187
00:24:18,610 --> 00:24:18,850
They came out.

188
00:24:21,910 --> 00:24:28,850
And they fell, uprooted, to the

189
00:24:30,060 --> 00:24:30,780
ground.

190
00:24:32,330 --> 00:24:34,750
[Listen. He quotes a Sanskrit phrase for the Lord's great strength, and the wording is unclear.]

191
00:24:38,440 --> 00:24:46,660
The Lord was pulling at the center of His great strength, so they came out

192
00:24:46,760 --> 00:24:50,240
as if a little piece of grass had been pulled up.

193
00:24:55,840 --> 00:25:01,500
He pulled with tremendous force. But

194
00:25:03,580 --> 00:25:10,940
the Lord did not take a huge form. He did not become like Nrisingha.

195
00:25:12,590 --> 00:25:15,110
This is the beauty of the child pastime.

196
00:25:21,200 --> 00:25:29,490
He was pulling, and the uprooted mortar was following along with Him.

197
00:25:29,490 --> 00:25:37,610
It was going behind Him. As He

198
00:25:37,610 --> 00:25:40,290
went slowly, the mortar went too.

199
00:25:42,100 --> 00:25:49,980
Then, when that Damodara child pulled it and gave a little strong tug,

200
00:25:50,120 --> 00:25:56,920
a jerk, from that alone both trees were uprooted.

201
00:25:58,230 --> 00:26:00,330
Their roots came out completely.

202
00:26:03,390 --> 00:26:12,060
They fell. When the Lord uprooted the trees,

203
00:26:12,090 --> 00:26:20,610
their big branches and their small twigs all began to shake. When a tree

204
00:26:20,610 --> 00:26:23,950
is being uprooted, the tree shakes, doesn't it? They shook greatly.

205
00:26:25,940 --> 00:26:35,300
And both

206
00:26:43,910 --> 00:26:50,710
had very thick branches, full of leaves, and fruit was also on them.

207
00:26:53,510 --> 00:26:55,650
These are Arjuna trees.

208
00:26:57,420 --> 00:27:05,380
You must have seen them. Doctors tell people to drink a preparation of their bark.

209
00:27:06,140 --> 00:27:08,400
It is a medicine for heart disease.

210
00:27:17,450 --> 00:27:24,490
[Listen, around 27:17. He quotes the verse about the branches shaking with a loud sound. The Sanskrit is unclear.] So

211
00:27:25,480 --> 00:27:33,740
the thick branches and the small twigs all began to shake, making a fierce sound,

212
00:27:33,740 --> 00:27:37,840
a tremendous sound, and both trees fell. And

213
00:27:39,320 --> 00:27:42,380
another wonder appeared there.

214
00:27:44,100 --> 00:27:46,960
At that time,

215
00:27:49,480 --> 00:27:57,710
when the trees were uprooted, a sight appeared there. A very great light,

216
00:27:57,710 --> 00:28:06,130
a very astonishing light, came out from the roots of these trees,

217
00:28:06,220 --> 00:28:07,600
from those

218
00:28:11,620 --> 00:28:16,300
two trees a very great light came out,

219
00:28:21,100 --> 00:28:23,820
a light like millions of suns.

220
00:28:29,710 --> 00:28:35,710
After that it became clear that they were very beautiful persons, very radiant.

221
00:28:37,080 --> 00:28:44,460
And coming out of the trees, those two came to the Lord, who

222
00:28:45,100 --> 00:28:51,520
was tied to the mortar. They were offering obeisances to the Lord who was tied to the mortar.

223
00:28:56,180 --> 00:29:00,180
They offered obeisances with the head, keeping the head on the ground.

224
00:29:06,320 --> 00:29:14,350
[Listen, around 29:06. He quotes "krishnam pranamya shirasa." The Sanskrit around it is unclear.] Lord Krishna is the Lord of all

225
00:29:14,350 --> 00:29:20,320
the worlds. People offered obeisances to such a Lord. They

226
00:29:21,660 --> 00:29:29,910
became free of every kind of sin and offense. They became clean. Their pride and their sin all

227
00:29:29,910 --> 00:29:32,690
left. They became pure. With hands

228
00:29:36,440 --> 00:29:44,030
folded, "Please forgive us." They began to say this to the Lord. They began to praise the Lord. They

229
00:29:45,890 --> 00:29:53,810
had been freed. When a soul is in his own true nature, he is very radiant.

230
00:29:57,490 --> 00:30:05,530
We read that when Lord Indra killed Vritrasura, from Vritrasura's body

231
00:30:05,530 --> 00:30:13,610
a wonderful light came out. Lighting all the directions, it finally

232
00:30:13,610 --> 00:30:15,650
entered the Lord's feet.

233
00:30:18,950 --> 00:30:27,540
A soul also has great radiance. When these two, Nalakuvara and Manigriva, were freed, a great light came from them.

234
00:30:27,540 --> 00:30:36,000
They appeared in a radiant form and began to pray to the Lord,

235
00:30:36,000 --> 00:30:36,600
to pray.

236
00:30:41,910 --> 00:30:44,670
At this point, one

237
00:30:46,050 --> 00:30:53,390
devotee has written a commentary, and I want to say one or two things.

238
00:30:55,310 --> 00:31:03,740
When the Lord was tied to the mortar, bound, at that time He delivered

239
00:31:03,740 --> 00:31:06,840
Nalakuvara and Manigriva. So

240
00:31:08,920 --> 00:31:17,340
what is the mood of this? He Himself was bound, and He freed others. And

241
00:31:17,340 --> 00:31:25,570
He was a child, a small child, and at that time He was delivering them. What is the reason? What message is He giving?

242
00:31:27,560 --> 00:31:31,320
[Listen. A commentator's name here is unclear.] They write that the main thing is

243
00:31:42,900 --> 00:31:48,510
one's own feeling, in this world.

244
00:31:51,490 --> 00:32:00,440
About one's own deliverance, in this material world, if a person thinks about deliverance,

245
00:32:00,440 --> 00:32:02,880
he has to do it himself. So he himself

246
00:32:05,160 --> 00:32:12,650
should do it. And the main thing is faith, feeling, toward Lord Krishna.

247
00:32:13,520 --> 00:32:18,140
As a person's feeling is, that is how his movement will be.

248
00:32:22,310 --> 00:32:28,080
By Narada's mercy, Nalakuvara had come to know the truth of the Lord.

249
00:32:29,620 --> 00:32:37,980
The Lord is bound, and still He is delivering them. By this the Lord is, as it were, teaching

250
00:32:37,980 --> 00:32:43,880
that it does not matter whether the guru is bound or free.

251
00:32:45,320 --> 00:32:53,740
The student must keep faith.

252
00:32:53,740 --> 00:33:00,220
And his deliverance will come from his own feeling. It comes from feeling for Krishna. And

253
00:33:07,480 --> 00:33:08,880
Krishna is bound.

254
00:33:11,600 --> 00:33:19,600
But Nalakuvara and Manigriva were thinking, "This is the Lord. He has descended.

255
00:33:20,030 --> 00:33:26,480
He is performing pastimes in Braj." By that feeling for the Lord, they became free.

256
00:33:31,680 --> 00:33:39,710
So, in this way, if a person is a devotee of the Lord, and if he is a guru, then about him

257
00:33:39,710 --> 00:33:51,250
one should not think too much, about whether

258
00:33:55,920 --> 00:33:59,620
deliverance comes from one's own great feeling for Krishna.

259
00:34:04,100 --> 00:34:12,220
And Narada had blessed them, in the form of a curse. In this way

260
00:34:12,220 --> 00:34:13,760
this

261
00:34:16,130 --> 00:34:21,240
is Narada's blessing for any

262
00:34:23,030 --> 00:34:24,110
soul.

263
00:34:32,590 --> 00:34:40,270
In the world there are many gurus, especially devotees of Lord Krishna,

264
00:34:42,480 --> 00:34:50,360
who are not all the same. They are not all equal in knowledge, or equally

265
00:34:50,900 --> 00:34:59,470
far from bad habits. Still, if a person takes their shelter,

266
00:34:59,470 --> 00:35:01,130
his good comes.

267
00:35:03,210 --> 00:35:05,550
This is the message the Lord is giving.

268
00:35:07,760 --> 00:35:14,500
Even while bound, Krishna delivered both trees. Srila

269
00:35:19,590 --> 00:35:21,670
Prabhupada has many disciples.

270
00:35:24,140 --> 00:35:32,540
But it is undoubtedly true that there will never be anyone equal to Srila Prabhupada.

271
00:35:32,540 --> 00:35:39,960
He was an associate of the Lord. He came carrying the Lord's power,

272
00:35:41,620 --> 00:35:49,720
to correct the world, to make everyone a devotee. But his disciples follow

273
00:35:49,720 --> 00:35:58,340
him, and they also preach, everywhere. It is true that they

274
00:35:58,340 --> 00:36:05,160
cannot be equal to Prabhupada. But by Prabhupada's mercy they

275
00:36:06,470 --> 00:36:09,730
deliver the souls of the world.

276
00:36:10,980 --> 00:36:13,380
And that does happen.

277
00:36:19,040 --> 00:36:27,400
Therefore one should keep faith in whoever one's guru is.

278
00:36:27,400 --> 00:36:33,600
By faith we will be delivered. Our rescue will come.

279
00:36:37,150 --> 00:36:44,300
One should not dwell on the guru's small faults.

280
00:36:45,620 --> 00:36:52,990
Here the Lord Himself is bound by His own act. What was that act? He had broken the pot.

281
00:36:53,710 --> 00:37:01,820
He had committed an offense, and Yashoda tied Him. And even the bound Lord delivered

282
00:37:01,820 --> 00:37:11,480
them. He freed

283
00:37:13,880 --> 00:37:21,430
them. The main thing is one's feeling, feeling for Krishna, and faith in the guru.

284
00:37:28,500 --> 00:37:34,600
He Himself is tied, and He delivered both trees.

285
00:37:37,700 --> 00:37:45,710
So even with some weakness, a devotee of the Lord can deliver someone else.

286
00:37:45,710 --> 00:37:46,590
He can.

287
00:37:47,450 --> 00:37:51,630
By Narada's mercy, by Srila Prabhupada's mercy,

288
00:37:53,330 --> 00:37:57,530
we have received Prabhupada's mercy.

289
00:37:59,320 --> 00:38:07,500
From his words it is clear that Srila Prabhupada

290
00:38:07,500 --> 00:38:15,960
wanted certain things to be done. In one place he says, "If

291
00:38:15,960 --> 00:38:21,060
you want to please me, then

292
00:38:24,980 --> 00:38:33,480
if you want to please me, make me happy, make me joyful, then distribute my books."

293
00:38:33,480 --> 00:38:34,160
Distribute them.

294
00:38:35,500 --> 00:38:44,530
This is a completely clear sentence. There is no doubt that if we distribute Prabhupada's

295
00:38:44,530 --> 00:38:52,300
books, Bhagavad-gita As It Is and his other books,

296
00:38:53,580 --> 00:38:59,400
we are pleasing Prabhupada. And if Prabhupada is pleased,

297
00:39:02,000 --> 00:39:08,060
our deliverance will happen. There is no doubt.

298
00:39:18,260 --> 00:39:24,340
So the message here is that feeling is the main thing, faith,

299
00:39:32,120 --> 00:39:40,090
and firm trust in the Lord, trust in Srila Prabhupada,

300
00:39:40,520 --> 00:39:48,670
trust in the parampara, and trust in one's own guru. Keeping that, one should practice

301
00:39:48,670 --> 00:39:55,420
Krishna consciousness. Then success will surely come, even if it takes time.

302
00:39:57,080 --> 00:40:05,250
But success does come. As Narada said, after one hundred years of the demigods they would

303
00:40:05,250 --> 00:40:14,020
meet the Lord. They would be near Him. It was a long time, but it was not darkness.

304
00:40:14,020 --> 00:40:22,020
By the Lord's mercy that time came, when they saw the Lord directly.

305
00:40:22,020 --> 00:40:23,380
And

306
00:40:25,870 --> 00:40:34,620
the Lord is a child when He delivers them. The lesson in this is that any person who is

307
00:40:34,620 --> 00:40:41,890
a devotee of the Lord brings good to others, whether he is a child or a young man. There is no

308
00:40:43,240 --> 00:40:52,060
rule about this. It is not that one becomes a guru only when every hair on the head has turned white.

309
00:40:53,150 --> 00:40:57,210
A young man can be a guru. A child can be a guru.

310
00:40:58,750 --> 00:41:02,230
This child delivered Nalakuvara and Manigriva.

311
00:41:04,960 --> 00:41:13,090
So many old cowherd men were walking around. They did nothing. One small child, in a moment, delivered

312
00:41:13,090 --> 00:41:17,460
the trees. This is the Lord's message.

313
00:41:19,740 --> 00:41:29,040
Whether a child, a young man, or an old man, one who knows the truth of Krishna is a real guru. He can deliver.

314
00:41:29,040 --> 00:41:29,980
He can.

315
00:41:32,120 --> 00:41:40,320
A son can deliver his father. Suppose the father is sick and cannot come to a program for the Lord.

316
00:41:40,320 --> 00:41:48,380
He cannot practice Krishna consciousness. If the child sits beside him and chants the Lord's name, Hare Krishna, Hare

317
00:41:48,380 --> 00:41:53,720
Krishna, Krishna Krishna, Hare Hare, Hare Rama, Hare Rama,

318
00:41:56,370 --> 00:42:03,870
then why will he not be delivered? By hearing the Lord's name, or by taking the Lord's prasadam and eating it,

319
00:42:04,860 --> 00:42:13,020
or if the child reads something about the Lord and lets his father hear it, why will the father not be delivered?

320
00:42:13,020 --> 00:42:18,600
The father may think, "What can this child make me hear?"

321
00:42:23,500 --> 00:42:25,700
There are Srila Prabhupada's books.

322
00:42:26,980 --> 00:42:31,820
Especially Bhagavad-gita As It Is.

323
00:42:33,740 --> 00:42:39,100
By reading it and hearing it, a very great result comes.

324
00:42:42,140 --> 00:42:48,460
This is why the Lord, in the form of a child, delivered Nalakuvara and Manigriva.

325
00:42:54,440 --> 00:43:02,740
They had committed an offense in an easygoing way, and they were tied, so they were dragging the mortar.

326
00:43:02,740 --> 00:43:09,120
Every one of us souls is bound like this, in the bondage of karma.

327
00:43:15,140 --> 00:43:21,240
We are bound, and we want our own deliverance.

328
00:43:24,030 --> 00:43:32,100
Then people think, "How will another person who is himself bound deliver anyone?"

329
00:43:32,100 --> 00:43:40,210
He will do it the way Krishna did it. Everyone is bound. So what if one is bound?

330
00:43:40,930 --> 00:43:49,030
One can still chant the Lord's name, offer obeisances to the Lord, and by the Lord's name, by the Lord's prasadam, and

331
00:43:49,030 --> 00:43:54,440
by the Lord's katha, anyone can be delivered.

332
00:43:59,370 --> 00:44:08,070
So one should not think too much about the guru's situation. One should keep

333
00:44:08,070 --> 00:44:10,570
faith. Benefit comes from faith.

334
00:44:12,360 --> 00:44:20,620
Many people say that only a first-class man of the Bhagavatam, only a topmost

335
00:44:20,620 --> 00:44:24,100
qualified person, can rescue others.

336
00:44:26,790 --> 00:44:33,210
The example is also there: a topmost person truly pulls people out of this world. But

337
00:44:34,550 --> 00:44:39,970
a bound soul can also deliver someone else.

338
00:44:43,680 --> 00:44:49,460
From the Lord's pastimes we get many kinds of hints.

339
00:44:54,060 --> 00:45:01,530
One should not think, "Only when a guru becomes like Srila Prabhupada will anyone be delivered."

340
00:45:02,880 --> 00:45:11,180
There is no need of that. The special quality in Prabhupada's disciples is devotion to the Lord.

341
00:45:11,980 --> 00:45:20,500
That same special quality is also in Prabhupada's grand-disciples. They too can do good for the world,

342
00:45:20,500 --> 00:45:22,680
and they are doing it.

343
00:45:25,640 --> 00:45:31,280
Faith is the main thing. If there is faith in Srila Prabhupada,

344
00:45:33,040 --> 00:45:34,680
they are also growing.

345
00:45:36,700 --> 00:45:39,020
It has been seen all over the world.

346
00:45:40,880 --> 00:45:44,060
The principle is this:

347
00:45:45,600 --> 00:45:49,200
by faith, deliverance happens.

348
00:45:51,370 --> 00:45:59,320
There is a story in the Mahabharata. The Mahabharata is the true history of Bharat. In that

349
00:46:01,850 --> 00:46:07,910
Mahabharata a story comes. Once, in the forest of Hastinapura,

350
00:46:11,940 --> 00:46:14,000
when, in Hastinapura,

351
00:46:20,030 --> 00:46:25,400
a teacher was appointed for them in archery.

352
00:46:27,280 --> 00:46:35,890
The princes were kshatriyas, the Kauravas and the Pandavas. To teach them, Bhishma Pitamaha appointed, for the bow,

353
00:46:35,890 --> 00:46:42,390
Dronacharya in charge. Dronacharya was a great brahmana, and

354
00:46:44,020 --> 00:46:45,780
a great master of the bow.

355
00:46:46,680 --> 00:46:50,920
He had learned archery from Lord Parashurama.

356
00:46:51,330 --> 00:46:53,670
Directly from the Lord.

357
00:46:53,930 --> 00:47:01,580
And the Lord had ordered him not to give this archery

358
00:47:05,550 --> 00:47:07,150
to a low person.

359
00:47:08,680 --> 00:47:16,890
"You may give it fully to kshatriyas. You may teach brahmanas, and you may teach kshatriyas.

360
00:47:16,890 --> 00:47:25,660
But do not give it to people below the kshatriyas." That was the Lord's order. So

361
00:47:26,110 --> 00:47:34,250
Dronacharya was keeping that order. Then one day a Bhil came to him,

362
00:47:34,570 --> 00:47:37,490
a Bhil, meaning a man of a forest tribe.

363
00:47:39,320 --> 00:47:46,520
He offered obeisances to Dronacharya and said, "We also want to learn archery."

364
00:47:47,440 --> 00:47:55,520
Dronacharya asked, "Who are you?" He said, "I am a Bhil." Dronacharya said, "Then you will do a hunter's work.

365
00:47:55,520 --> 00:48:02,810
You can learn this archery from someone else. I will not teach you."

366
00:48:07,230 --> 00:48:15,680
But that person was firm in his decision. He had settled it in his mind

367
00:48:15,680 --> 00:48:23,990
that Dronacharya alone would be his guru, and from him he would learn archery. He was very disappointed. Dronacharya

368
00:48:23,990 --> 00:48:31,650
did not teach him. He did not teach him the science of the bow. So he went home.

369
00:48:32,670 --> 00:48:40,060
His home was in the forest itself, a broken little house. In it

370
00:48:41,880 --> 00:48:47,880
he made a deity of Dronacharya, and from that deity he began to learn.

371
00:48:50,730 --> 00:48:58,740
He had very strong faith, a deep love for Dronacharya.

372
00:48:58,740 --> 00:49:05,860
He learned from him in that way: how to use the bow, and even how to recite the mantras, and everything.

373
00:49:11,400 --> 00:49:17,960
And Dronacharya had told Arjuna, "You will become the greatest archer in the world."

374
00:49:19,300 --> 00:49:29,080
You

375
00:49:29,270 --> 00:49:30,170
so

376
00:49:31,740 --> 00:49:38,080
Arjuna, Yudhishthira, Bhima, and the others were all with him. So

377
00:49:40,420 --> 00:49:49,450
a dog also came out of Hastinapura with them, and went into the forest. The dog went to

378
00:49:49,580 --> 00:49:57,780
Ekalavya's house. That Bhil's name was Ekalavya. There it began to bark, and he was learning

379
00:49:57,780 --> 00:50:05,920
archery with full attention. The barking disturbed him. So, to stop the dog's

380
00:50:05,920 --> 00:50:08,180
voice,

381
00:50:10,720 --> 00:50:18,780
he shot arrows from the bow. The dog was barking, so into its mouth

382
00:50:18,780 --> 00:50:27,100
he shot arrows and filled the whole mouth. The mouth was filled, so the dog

383
00:50:27,100 --> 00:50:28,860
could not speak. So

384
00:50:30,500 --> 00:50:38,670
then it came running back to the princes, to Arjuna. Dronacharya was also there.

385
00:50:38,670 --> 00:50:39,890
So

386
00:50:41,330 --> 00:50:49,530
Arjuna saw it and was astonished. He even asked, "Guruji, to which person

387
00:50:49,530 --> 00:50:57,740
have you taught this skill? We do not even know this. At a dog

388
00:50:57,740 --> 00:51:05,820
he has shot an arrow so that the arrow did not cut the tongue and did not peel the gum. There was no wound

389
00:51:05,820 --> 00:51:14,200
anywhere. Only the mouth was filled. Now think about it. To shoot an arrow so that it only goes into the mouth

390
00:51:14,200 --> 00:51:20,460
and stays there, and fills it, with no pain. The dog's voice had only been stopped.

391
00:51:32,940 --> 00:51:41,000
Then, by means of that dog, the dog started to run. When they chased it, they went the way it was running.

392
00:51:41,000 --> 00:51:43,040
Wherever it was going, they went.

393
00:51:44,800 --> 00:51:50,160
The dog kept going, and there was a cottage, Ekalavya's house.

394
00:51:52,150 --> 00:52:00,520
There was a deity of Dronacharya, which Ekalavya himself had made. He was not a great artist.

395
00:52:00,680 --> 00:52:07,660
He had made the deity somehow, and he was learning archery through that deity.

396
00:52:10,000 --> 00:52:13,460
Then Dronacharya asked,

397
00:52:14,930 --> 00:52:23,000
"Did you shoot the arrow at this dog?" He said, "Yes. By your mercy I have learned, and I shot it."

398
00:52:24,340 --> 00:52:26,820
Dronacharya asked, "From whom

399
00:52:29,350 --> 00:52:36,900
did you learn all this?" He said, "I am learning from you."

400
00:52:39,230 --> 00:52:47,430
"You are learning from us? How, from us?" Then he showed the deity inside. "See, I made your

401
00:52:47,430 --> 00:52:51,070
deity, and I am learning from it.

402
00:52:52,480 --> 00:52:54,880
I have learned all this from you."

403
00:52:56,800 --> 00:53:04,800
Then at the end Dronacharya said, this talk is long, "Do you accept me as guru?"

404
00:53:04,800 --> 00:53:09,290
And Ekalavya said, "Yes."

405
00:53:13,000 --> 00:53:15,800
"Then can you give some guru-dakshina?"

406
00:53:17,910 --> 00:53:20,090
He said, "Yes. Please order me."

407
00:53:22,060 --> 00:53:30,220
Dronacharya said, "Cut off the thumb of your right hand and give it to me." That was the only order.

408
00:53:30,220 --> 00:53:34,240
And as soon as he received the order, he cut off the thumb with a sword and gave it.

409
00:53:40,540 --> 00:53:48,630
This is called nistha, firm faith. He had such faith in the guru that, just because the guru asked,

410
00:53:48,630 --> 00:53:54,210
he gave his thumb. It is with this thumb that an arrow is shot on the bow.

411
00:53:58,050 --> 00:54:06,660
Whatever the social consideration was, that kshatriyas should be the ones

412
00:54:06,660 --> 00:54:11,870
to become expert in archery, for that Dronacharya asked for Ekalavya's thumb. And

413
00:54:16,030 --> 00:54:24,180
it was Lord Parashurama's order, so Dronacharya did all this. But see the greatness of Ekalavya.

414
00:54:24,280 --> 00:54:25,320
He gave it.

415
00:54:26,640 --> 00:54:33,240
And after that he could not shoot the bow and arrow. And

416
00:54:35,670 --> 00:54:43,710
the main point is this. By making a deity of Dronacharya, he could become such an expert archer.

417
00:54:44,890 --> 00:54:53,050
That is a material skill. This, our practice, is a spiritual skill. It is our own nature. If someone becomes expert in it, what

418
00:54:53,050 --> 00:55:01,920
is surprising? And there is Prabhupada's murti. It is not only Prabhupada's murti. Prabhupada

419
00:55:01,920 --> 00:55:03,460
also speaks.

420
00:55:05,600 --> 00:55:13,530
He gives lectures. His lectures are there. His books are there. So why can we not succeed?

421
00:55:13,790 --> 00:55:22,610
When Ekalavya, by making a deity of Dronacharya, became such a great archer,

422
00:55:24,080 --> 00:55:32,170
then devotion to the Lord is our own nature. If we take Srila Prabhupada as the ideal

423
00:55:32,170 --> 00:55:36,630
and want his mercy, why will we not receive it?

424
00:55:40,050 --> 00:55:48,310
This is a true event. It is not made up. The Mahabharata is a great book, and anyone who wants to read it

425
00:55:48,310 --> 00:55:49,570
can read it.

426
00:55:53,380 --> 00:56:01,560
The Bhagavad-gita is a part of that same Mahabharata. It is a scripture of the sages. False stories are not put in it.

427
00:56:01,560 --> 00:56:09,100
It is true history. So this is the story of one boy, Ekalavya.

428
00:56:09,900 --> 00:56:18,320
[Listen, around 56:09. The sentence breaks off. He is still speaking of Ekalavya.]

429
00:56:18,770 --> 00:56:26,940
Knowing he was not a kshatriya, Drona did not teach him. And still, by his own faith, he received such

430
00:56:26,940 --> 00:56:32,210
great teaching and became a great archer.

431
00:56:34,410 --> 00:56:36,750
From this we learn that

432
00:56:39,830 --> 00:56:46,180
when there is great faith in the guru,

433
00:56:48,990 --> 00:56:52,550
a person reaches success in devotion to the Lord.

434
00:56:54,190 --> 00:57:03,070
As our effort is, and as our faith is, that is the success we will receive. The Lord

435
00:57:03,070 --> 00:57:04,690
also says in the Gita,

436
00:57:08,910 --> 00:57:17,150
one should deliver oneself by oneself. One should not throw oneself into misery and worry.

437
00:57:18,590 --> 00:57:23,470
A person's deliverance is in his own hands.

438
00:57:26,510 --> 00:57:28,930
What is the use of only having a very big guru?

439
00:57:31,960 --> 00:57:40,000
Prabhupada gave initiation, he gave the process, he gave instruction. If someone does not chant the maha-mantra, and

440
00:57:40,000 --> 00:57:45,410
does not keep himself ready inside, what will he do? Even after

441
00:57:49,280 --> 00:57:56,890
taking initiation from a very high guru, if a person is careless, he cannot be corrected. And

442
00:57:59,680 --> 00:58:08,780
if he learns devotion from an ordinary person, but he is eager,

443
00:58:08,780 --> 00:58:13,520
he has attachment and faith, then that person reaches success.

444
00:58:17,770 --> 00:58:24,550
When the Lord performs pastimes, there are many hints in those pastimes.

445
00:58:27,140 --> 00:58:35,270
Even in a bound condition the Lord delivered Nalakuvara and Manigriva. In truth

446
00:58:35,270 --> 00:58:42,180
the Lord is never bound. But He is visibly bound. Mother Yashoda tied Him.

447
00:58:44,150 --> 00:58:47,870
He is tied, and still He delivered them.

448
00:58:49,830 --> 00:58:55,470
One should always keep this scene in the mind.

449
00:58:59,340 --> 00:59:02,180
How charming the Lord is. From that

450
00:59:03,650 --> 00:59:11,350
very day the gopis, Yashoda's friends, started calling Him Damodara.

451
00:59:12,340 --> 00:59:20,660
They would call Him that, and even in a teasing way they would say Damodara. If someone said, "This Damodara,"

452
00:59:20,660 --> 00:59:29,720
it meant, "Hey, thief, butter thief, rascal." Damodara means the one

453
00:59:29,980 --> 00:59:33,080
around whose belly the rope was tied.

454
00:59:34,530 --> 00:59:43,320
When someone said it, Krishna would feel a little hurt. This is also His pastime. Once Mother

455
00:59:43,320 --> 00:59:47,740
Rohini went to call Him for eating. He was playing.

456
00:59:50,440 --> 00:59:57,950
Mother Rohini said, "Damodara, come and eat." He did not go. Inside,

457
00:59:58,820 --> 01:00:04,740
He was not happy. "She is My mother, and she is calling Me like this."

458
01:00:06,910 --> 01:00:12,120
When Yashoda went, she did not say Damodara.

459
01:00:14,350 --> 01:00:22,570
On the same day the rope was tied, when Yashoda went, He came to eat. He did not come when Rohini called,

460
01:00:23,110 --> 01:00:26,770
because she had said "Damodara."

461
01:00:28,310 --> 01:00:36,790
From any act, a person gets honor or gets a bad name. This name was pointing to a wrong act of Krishna,

462
01:00:36,920 --> 01:00:44,960
the name of one around whose belly a rope

463
01:00:44,960 --> 01:00:48,180
had been tied. And why was it tied? One

464
01:00:50,130 --> 01:00:57,190
day He had done such mischief. He had broken the pot of yogurt at home, so His mother tied Him.

465
01:01:00,280 --> 01:01:06,670
And nobody else. His own mother is so good-hearted that Mother tied Him.

466
01:01:12,470 --> 01:01:28,250
Whatever it is, even if there is some hurt, Krishna is still fine. And even today, by saying Damodara,

467
01:01:34,210 --> 01:01:36,610
it is a very dear name.

468
01:01:38,150 --> 01:01:44,010
One should keep a picture of such Damodara, the Lord, in the heart. [Listen. The last few words trail off.]
